WEBVTT

00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:04.693
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> At least half of your daily liquids should come from water.

00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:13.677
About one third – or three to four cups – can come from coffee or tea – but with no sugar.

00:00:14.861 --> 00:00:18.649
Low-fat milk can make up another twenty per cent.

00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:23.815
If you drink less milk, just try to get your calcium from

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:28.556
another type of food or drink, for example, green vegetables.

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:33.612
You can have one small glass of fruit juice a day,

00:00:34.462 --> 00:00:40.609
and no more than one to two alcoholic drinks for men, or one for women.

00:00:41.822 --> 00:00:48.649
However, some doctors now think that it’s a good idea to have several alcohol-free days a week.

00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:54.519
Diet drinks, which use artificial sweeteners, are not good for you,

00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:58.447
but up to one to two glasses a day is OK.

00:00:59.508 --> 00:01:06.322
But try not to have any drinks with a lot of sugar, for example, sweet fizzy drinks.